<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Projects | Mark Boss</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/</link><atom:link href="https://markboss.me/projects/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><description>Projects</description><generator>HugoBlox Kit (https://hugoblox.com)</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 17 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://markboss.me/media/icon_hu_305902ed81759b07.png</url><title>Projects</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/</link></image><item><title>Postergeist</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/postergeist/</link><pubDate>Tue, 17 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/postergeist/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Outline.md</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/outline_md/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/outline_md/</guid><description/></item><item><title>GifDrop</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/gifdrop/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/gifdrop/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Citegeist</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/citegeist/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/citegeist/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Geotex</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/geotex/</link><pubDate>Mon, 12 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/geotex/</guid><description/></item><item><title>PyNanoInstantMeshes</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/pynanoinstantmeshes/</link><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/pynanoinstantmeshes/</guid><description/></item><item><title>TLCyzer</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/tlcyzer/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Aug 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/tlcyzer/</guid><description/></item><item><title>farrow-and-ball</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/farrow-and-ball/</link><pubDate>Mon, 28 Jun 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/farrow-and-ball/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Online BRDF Visualization</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/web_brdf_viz/</link><pubDate>Tue, 01 Dec 2020 10:32:39 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/web_brdf_viz/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A bidirectional reflectance distribution function (BRDF) is a function which defines how incoming light $\omega_i$ is reflected to every outgoing direction $\omega_o$ on the hemisphere $f_r(\omega_i, \omega_o)$. A BRDF can be measured by capturing a surface from various known view and light positions. The information can then be stored in a texture where the x and y coordinates represent the corresponding view and light direction. This is mostly only done for materials that do not vary over the surface due to the information density. Therefore, often analytical BRDF models are used. Parameters are then used to build a function that can be queried for all incoming and outgoing directions. One popular model is the &lt;a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/357290.357293" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Cook-Torrance&lt;/a&gt; model, which parametrizes the BRDF with a diffuse and specular color plus a roughness value. The model is split into a diffuse and specular lobe. Below is an interactive visualizer, where you can change the diffuse, specular, and roughness parameters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="width: 100%; padding-top: 100%; position: relative;"&gt;
&lt;iframe src="https://markboss.me/files/brdf_viz/brdf_eval.html" width="100%" height="100%" frameborder=" 0 " style="position: absolute; top: 0;
left: 0;
bottom: 0;
right: 0;"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interpolating between random BRDFs is also quite soothing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="width: 100%; padding-top: 100%; position: relative;"&gt;
&lt;iframe src="https://markboss.me/files/brdf_viz/brdf_eval.html?rngesus=1" width="100%" height="100%" frameborder=" 0 " style="position: absolute; top: 0;
left: 0;
bottom: 0;
right: 0;"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to use this interactive visualizer for teaching, feel free to use it: &lt;a href="https://markboss.me/files/brdf_viz/brdf_eval.html"&gt;link&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Infomark</title><link>https://markboss.me/projects/infomark/</link><pubDate>Sat, 28 Dec 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://markboss.me/projects/infomark/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>